course: dictionary
lesson: 4211
title: The word government
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A government is the group of people who run a country, a state or a city. They make decisions about laws, taxes and services. «Governments, companies, scientists and ordinary people all have a say in the rules for AI, through laws, votes and choices.» Here the government is one of the groups that help make the rules.
explain: Governments do many jobs. They make laws, collect taxes and pay for schools, hospitals, roads and the police. When you read about a government, ask: what is it deciding, and who does it affect? The clues around the word will often tell you which kind of government is meant.
explain: The word can also mean the way a country is ruled. Countries have different forms of government. Some have a president, some have a prime minister, and some have a parliament or congress. In a democracy, people vote to choose the government. «The capital was put outside every state so that no single state would control the national government.»
fact: A government is the group of people who run a country, state or city.
fact: Governments make laws, collect taxes and pay for schools, hospitals, roads and the police.
fact: In a democracy, people vote to choose their government.
fact: Different countries have different governments: a president, a prime minister, a parliament or a congress.
fact: «Local government» runs a town or city, and «federal government» runs a whole country that is made of states.
exercise: «Governments, companies, scientists and ordinary people all have a say in the rules for AI.» What is a government? | A group of friends who play games | *The group of people who run a country and make its laws | A scientist who studies the weather | A company that sells computers
exercise: «The capital was put outside every state so that no single state would control the national government.» What does national government mean here? | *The people who run the whole country | A garden in the middle of the city | A shop that sells flags for every state | The price of food in the shops
exercise: «Some say governments spent and printed too much money.» Find and copy one word that means the groups that run countries. | others | *governments | pandemic | money
test: In a democracy, how do people help choose their government? | By voting | *By voting in elections | By sleeping late on Sundays | By counting trees in the park
test: Which jobs does a government do? | *Makes laws and pays for schools, hospitals and roads | Bakes bread for every family | Plays football for the whole country | Paints the pictures in museums
exam: In the phrase «form of government», what does government mean? | A gift that a person gives to a country | *The way a country is ruled | A building where the police work | A car that belongs to the president
